#: ../../gas_laws/index.rst:3
msgid "標準状態の気体の体積"
msgstr "Gas Volume at Standard Temperature and Pressure (0 °C, 1 atm)"

#: ../../gas_laws/index.rst:5
msgid ""
"「0 ℃、1気圧で気体1 molは約22.4 L」という関係を、\\ 小さな計算セルに入れた気体の運動と圧力から調べます。\\ "
"第1回ではArの体積を変え、第2回では分子の種類を変えて比較します。"
msgstr ""
"At 0 °C and 1 atm, one mole of gas occupies about 22.4 L. \\ We examine "
"this relationship through the motion and pressure of a gas in a small "
"simulation cell. \\ In Part 1, we vary the volume of Ar. In Part 2, we "
"compare different gas species."

#: ../../gas_laws/index.rst:11
msgid ":doc:`第1回 気体1 molはなぜ22.4 Lなのか？ <argon_molar_volume>`"
msgstr ""
":doc:`Part 1: Why Does One Mole of Gas Occupy 22.4 L? "
"<argon_molar_volume>`"

#: ../../gas_laws/index.rst:12
msgid ":doc:`第2回 気体の種類が違っても、1 molの体積はほぼ同じ？ <five_gases_avogadro>`"
msgstr ""
":doc:`Part 2: Do Different Gases Have Nearly the Same Volume per Mole? "
"<five_gases_avogadro>`"

